feat/upcloud-inference held the cost research (docs/ai-inference-costs.md),
the UpCloud and RunPod vLLM provisioning (infra/inference/upcloud, vllm) and
shim options for our own model behind a tunnel. The shim now has a primary
and a fallback upstream, so the tunnel options apply to each: an Access
service token (UPSTREAM_/FALLBACK_ACCESS_CLIENT_ID/SECRET), a Workers VPC
binding (UPSTREAM_/FALLBACK_VPC) and the per-pass vLLM cache salt
(UPSTREAM_/FALLBACK_CACHE_SALT), so either can be our own vLLM later. A pinned
model never stands in for a catalog model the catalog lists no id for (it
would be charged that model's multiplier).

The cost doc gains §15: the model menu, how each multiplier is computed from
real cost and the 1.25 margin, and today's lineup.

